  "key_findings": [
    "80 PRs merged to main in the window. Largest categories: Other 24 (Primus Projection backends, SpecForge, new model/recipe work for GLM-5.3, ZAYA1, Inkling, MI455X, AutoModel diffusion), Bug Fix 22, Performance Optimization 16, CI/Infra 8, Turbo/Dependency Version Update 6, Docs 3, Refactor 1.",
    "Megatron-LM pin CHANGED in-window via PR #1321 (merged 2026-10-29): third_party/Megatron-LM and primus/_thirdparty.lock moved d3528a21 (Core 0.16.0rc0) -> core_v0.19.2 release tag 4b4acac9 (committed 2026-09-18). This is a backend version/pin change, so the Megatron backend-gap report set was regenerated. backend_gap_updated = true.",
    "After the bump the Megatron pin (core_v0.19.2, 4b4acac9) is 1011 commits behind upstream main HEAD 037b883c (Core 0.21.0, 2026-11-01), down from ~1662 before the bump. The tree diff is 2722 files / 531548 insertions / 293033 deletions; the release tag carries 28 release-only commits not on main. Recommendation: plan sync.",
    "torchtitan pin UNCHANGED (73a0e697 = v0.2.2 tag, an ancestor of main). Upstream main advanced to d86c77d6 (2026-11-01), widening the gap from 1194 to 1537 commits; upstream assets/version.txt still declares 0.2.2. No TorchTitan backend-gap regeneration (pin did not move). Recommendation: plan sync.",
    "Primus-Turbo Q4 quarterly drift (quarter start 2026-10-01, anchor bc8fd627): the CI-tracked PRIMUS_TURBO_COMMIT advanced ae1ac068 -> d04ffd9b (+28 commits, 143 files), crossing tagged releases v0.6.0 and v0.6.1. Dependency pins bumped: AITER v0.1.14.post1 (0f3c58e6) -> v0.1.24.post1 (04896172), Triton 09500db9 -> fc8d31a5 (release/3.9.x, 3.9.0); UCCL unchanged (5afb4117). Recommendation: monitor.",
    "Turbo work landing this quarter underpins several in-window Primus PRs: Mega MoE memory sized to dispatched rows (#1271, Turbo #566/#568), GPT-OSS on MegaMoE with expert biases (#1285), FlyDSL kernels ported to the 0.3.x API (#1275), and tensorwise-FP8 Qwen3-30B-A3B on MI355X (#1247).",
    "Other in-window submodule movement with no backend-gap report set (noted, not regenerated): maxtext (PRs #1228, #1289) and Automodel (PR #1314); HunyuanWorld-Mirror-rocm added as a new submodule (PR #1242). Only Megatron-LM and torchtitan have backend-gap report sets, and only Megatron-LM changed.",
    "Notable Megatron compatibility follow-up: PR #1340 makes MegaMoE run on Megatron-LM core_v0.19.2 with PrimusTopKRouter, and Megatron-Bridge SFT fixes (#1291, #1297, #1298) landed alongside the core bump."
